"""RHC: elite-prefix resampling (destroy-and-repair on synthesis routes) + discounted-bandit behaviour portfolio
          + exact-budget dedupe, for the 3D compositional GFlowNet (3DSynthFlow / CGFlow).

Mechanism (see docs/RHC_PREFIX.md and docs/rhc/REPORT.md)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
* ModeTracker   keeps every docked molecule and the evaluation-protocol set of diverse top modes (QED > 0.5, ranked by Vina,
                greedy diversity rule of rxnflow.utils.chem_metrics.compute_diverse_top_k).  The first `elite_size` modes form the
                elite archive; "hits" are new members of the evaluated top-`k_modes` set.
* Prefix arm    a share of the 64 slots per iteration re-builds an elite synthesis route up to step k (forced, the pose flow is
                re-run from scratch) and lets the CURRENT policy complete it.  The offspring condition is drawn from the Bayesian
                posterior p(c | x_elite) ~ p(c) R_c(x_elite) / Z(c)  (self-normalised importance resampling from the prior).
                The trajectories enter the unchanged TB loss; the loss is valid for any full-support training distribution.
* Portfolio     discounted Thompson sampling over {on-policy, prefix-1, prefix-2} with per-call hit rates (floor / cap on shares).
* Dedupe        every docked score is cached; duplicates are not re-docked and the freed oracle calls are re-spent on extra
                on-policy samples so that exactly `num_from_policy` NOVEL molecules are docked per iteration.

Everything is default-off: with `rhc.enable=false` the trainer subclass takes the baseline code path.
"""
